{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790990553,"nonce":"qF9+OkP6FFszgovg/8lpjJpNx1w=","title":"Resolve inherited text colour in the paint walk, not by copying into props","message":"Today `props.text_color` holds both what a node set itself and what it\ninherited, because the inheritance passes copy the parent's value in\n(`p.text_color = p.text_color.or(inherited.color)`). Once copied, an\ninherited colour is indistinguishable from a set one, and two failures\nfollow:\n\n- content built after the pass has no colour until another pass runs,\n  which is the Stateful case in 9008028, worked around per widget;\n- when an ancestor's colour changes after the pass — theme switch,\n  `:hover`, a bound class — descendants keep the stale copy, because\n  `.or()` now sees a value.\n\nProposed, matching what ashui does in its own paint walk:\n\n- `props.text_color` holds only what a node set itself, from its own CSS\n  rule, `.color()` or a binding. The passes stop copying.\n- The paint walk carries the inherited colour down the layout tree:\n  `effective = own.or(inherited)`, and passes the effective value to\n  children. Text paints with `effective.unwrap_or(text_data.color)`.\n- That same inherited colour is SVG's `currentColor`, as in CSS, so an\n  icon inside `.text-error` is red.\n- `resolved_text_color` computes the effective value by walking\n  ancestors rather than reading props.\n\nEvery rebuild is then correct by construction: no pass to re-run and no\nper-widget workaround.\n\n\nProposed by the ashui session, which named three sites. There are four,\nand a second walk:\n\n1. `propagate_inherited_text`, renderer/stylesheet/base.rs — the\n   recursive carry-down.\n2. A tuple-passing loop in `apply_stylesheet_base_styles`, same file.\n   This is the path a `style { }` block in a `.blinc` file takes.\n3. A near-identical tuple loop in renderer/stylesheet/layout.rs.\n4. **renderer/build/text.rs** — inherits at BUILD time, and not only\n   colour: decoration, white-space, text-overflow, text-align, SVG fill\n   and SVG stroke. Not in the earlier count.\n\nAnd the read happens in two places, not one:\n\n- renderer/paint/layout_renderer.rs — `props.text_color.unwrap_or(text_data.color)`\n- **blinc_app/src/context.rs** — the same expression. If props stop\n  carrying inherited values, this walk needs the same carry-down or\n  blinc_app loses the colour instead.\n\n`blinc_cn/tests/badge_label_color.rs` asserts on `resolved_text_color`,\nso it pins the semantics and should keep passing.\n\n\nThe other `InheritedText` properties could move the same way, but\n`text-align` and `white-space` feed layout, so they likely have to stay\na pre-layout pass. Colour, decoration and SVG paint do not.\n\nSupersedes the symptom in 9008028.","files":null}]}